## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable, privacy-aware dimensionality reduction in a distributed, streaming, regulated context.

## Key Concepts
- Incremental PCA and federated aggregation
- Differential privacy (Gaussian mechanism, zCDP)
- Drift detection and interpretability of loadings
- Missing data handling and streaming updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch of federated DP-PCA
// Note: this is illustrative; actual implementation requires secure aggregation libraries
function federatedDpPca(localData) {
  const imputed = imputeMissing(localData);
  const cov = computeCovariance(imputed);
  const noisy = addDpNoise(cov, epsilon, delta);
  sendDeltaToAggregator(noisy);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you allocate privacy budget over time and components?
- How would you evaluate downstream task performance under DP constraints?

